('099dfcdd-9ae2-54ef-976c-bb2a4206bf4b', '451c0a56-584e-41c1-958b-7b940530308c', '1f9b9b3e-2978-4618-bfd5-4659023c5bdb', 'a-level', '24.5', '9702 coursebook 24.5 · Currents crossing fields', 42, 42, 'A lightning strike sends a current of 20 kA down a vertical lightning conductor 10 m tall. The Earth''s horizontal field there is 2.0 × 10⁻⁵ T. (a) Explain why only the horizontal component of the Earth''s field matters. (b) Calculate the force on the conductor. (c) State the direction of the force relative to the horizontal field. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '4', 'N', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) The vertical component is parallel to the conductor and gives no force. (b) F = BIL = 2.0 × 10⁻⁵ × 20 × 10³ × 10 = 4.0 N. (c) Horizontal and at right angles to the horizontal field (east or west depending on the current direction). Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: vertical component parallel. C1: F = BIL. C1: substitution. B1: direction perpendicular to B_h. A1: F = 4.0 N.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('3d0f891b-503e-5d41-b271-897e493a97b0', '451c0a56-584e-41c1-958b-7b940530308c', '1f9b9b3e-2978-4618-bfd5-4659023c5bdb', 'a-level', '24.5', '9702 coursebook 24.5 · Currents crossing fields', 43, 43, 'A wire PQR has PQ = 0.20 m along the +x direction and QR = 0.15 m along the +y direction. A uniform field of 0.40 T points in the +z direction, and a current of 5.0 A flows from P to R. (a) Calculate the force on PQ and state its direction. (b) Calculate the force on QR and state its direction. (c) Calculate the resultant force. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.5', 'N', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) F_PQ = 0.40 × 5.0 × 0.20 = 0.40 N, along −y. (b) F_QR = 0.40 × 5.0 × 0.15 = 0.30 N, along +x. (c) Resultant = √(0.40² + 0.30²) = 0.50 N. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: F on PQ. B1: direction −y. C1: F on QR. B1: direction +x. C1: resultant. A1: F = 0.50 N.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 360 260" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg9a6e4493-t fg9a6e4493-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg9a6e4493-t">Wire PQR</title><desc id="fg9a6e4493-d">A wire PQR: PQ = 0.20 m along +x and QR = 0.15 m along +y, carrying 5.0 A from P to R, in a uniform 0.40 T field along +z (out of the page).</desc><circle cx="34.2" cy="49.4" r="4.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="34.2" cy="49.4" r="1.6" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><circle cx="34.2" cy="88.2" r="4.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="34.2" cy="88.2" r="1.6" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><circle cx="34.2" cy="127" r="4.5" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="34.2" cy="127" r