one;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="90" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">6</text><line x1="20" y1="52.7" x2="24" y2="52.7" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="52.7" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">8</text><text x="203" y="234" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">d / cm</text><text x="20" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">(F/L) / 10⁻⁴ N m⁻¹</text><line x1="59.8" y1="48.7" x2="67.8" y2="56.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="59.8" y1="56.7" x2="67.8" y2="48.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="99.6" y1="123.3" x2="107.6" y2="131.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="99.6" y1="131.3" x2="107.6" y2="123.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="179.1" y1="160.7" x2="187.1" y2="168.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="179.1" y1="168.7" x2="187.1" y2="160.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="338.2" y1="179.3" x2="346.2" y2="187.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="338.2" y1="187.3" x2="346.2" y2="179.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></g></svg>', 'Table and graph of force per metre against separation for two wires with equal currents: d = 1.0, 2.0, 4.0, 8.0 cm give F/L = 8.0, 4.0, 2.0, 1.0 × 10⁻⁴ N m⁻¹, a falling curve.'),
('74b6537e-b5ea-5beb-9164-a18537823c67', '451c0a56-584e-41c1-958b-7b940530308c', '24441dab-5d68-43e9-91a5-25bd381ac0fa', 'a-level', '24.6', '9702 coursebook 24.6 · Forces between currents', 49, 49, 'A wire with a mass of 5.0 g per metre carries 20 A and lies 1.0 cm from a parallel wire also carrying 20 A. (a) Calculate the magnetic force per metre between the wires. (b) Calculate the weight per metre of the first wire. (c) Calculate (magnetic force) ÷ (weight). (F/L = µ₀I₁I₂/2πd.) Give only the answer to (c). Take µ₀/2π = 2.0 × 10⁻⁷ T m A⁻¹. Take g = 9.81 m s⁻².', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.1631', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) F/L = 2.0 × 10⁻⁷ × 20 × 20 ÷ 0.010 = 8.0 × 10⁻³ N m⁻¹. (b) W/L = 5.0 × 10⁻³ × 9.81 = 0.0491 N m⁻¹. (c) Ratio = 8.0 × 10⁻³ ÷ 0.04905 = 0.163. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: magnetic force per metre. C1: weight per metre. C1: ratio. B1: units consistent. A1: ratio = 0.163.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('560a6227-90c5-5aa5-8f0f-be3c25fab8b6', '451c0a56-584e-41c1-958b-7b940530308c', '24441dab-5d68-43e9-91a5-25bd381ac0fa', 'a-level', '24.6', '9702 coursebook 24.6 · Forces between currents', 50, 50, 'Two parallel beams of electrons move in the same direction at speed v. The magnetic attraction between them is smaller than their electric repulsion by a factor of v²/c². (a) Explain why the beams attract magnetically. (b) Calculate (magnetic force) ÷ (electric force) when v = 3.0 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹. (c) State what this implies for the beams. Give only the answer to (b). Take c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.01', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) Moving charges are currents; parallel currents in the same direction attract. (b) Ratio = (3.0 × 10⁷ ÷ 3.00 × 10⁸)² = 0.010. (c) The electric repulsion dominates, so the beams spread apart. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: beams are parallel currents. C1: v/c. C1: ratio. B1: beams diverge. A1: ratio = 0.010.', 5, NULL, NULL)
INSERT INTO problem_options (id, problem_id, option_text, option_letter, is_correct, "order") VALUES
('59147ccd-6539-51cb-b931-b9f477624a4d', '635ee459-8106-5cef-a3f2-0b54947d4dec', 'Their electric charges attract', 'A', false, 0),
('cafc40c0-1ce9-505e-81c5-9ad575720efc', '635ee459-8106-5cef-a3f2-0b54947d4dec', 'Their weights pull them together', 'B', false, 1),
('c20ac567-d8e5-51b9-9850-d6e613682d1d', '635ee459-8106-5cef-a3f2-0b54947d4dec', 'Each wire lies in the magnetic field of the other, so each carries a current in a field', 'C', true, 2),
('296df709-6bd4-5809-a622-acec72cef211', '635ee459-8106-5cef-a3f2-0b54947d4dec', 'The currents heat the air between them', 'D', false, 3),
('fdfd0123-5769-5faa-a733-17b4885ce457', '80a878e1-7fd8-5b2e-84d3-34a04abf2c35', 'They are equal in size and opposite in direction', 'A', true, 0),
('57da6f5f-95a6-577f-b11d-67c7d297924d', '80a878e1-7fd8-5b2e-84d3-34a04abf2c35', 'The force on the 8.0 A wire is four times larger', 'B', false, 1),
('c5b862f7-2297-547f-b266-7f253bd5eb80', '80a878e1-7fd8-5b2e-84d3-34a04abf2c35', 'The force on the 2.0 A wire is four times larger', 'C', false, 2),
('75909b6a-3e6b-5d61-aeb9-0715894cf9b3', '80a878e1-7fd8-5b2e-84d3-34a04abf2c35', 'Only the 8.0 A wire feels a force', 'D', false, 3),
('1438680e-38df-54aa-a2fd-35eb19e7daad', '9b06f17f-5e15-5298-939b-d0c9945ba52e', 'They attract more strongly', 'A', false, 0),
('ff9cf32c-fb06-5571-955e-625838358e43', '9b06f17f-5e15-5298-939b-d0c9945ba52e', 'The force becomes zero', 'B', false, 1),
('9dccbb76-8fa5-520d-808d-bde9bd193d77', '9b06f17f-5e15-5298-939b-d0c9945ba52e', 'They still attract with the same force', 'C', false, 2),
('61cf9fa9-da97-5c95-bf54-cafc769937c0', '9b06f17f-5e15-5298-939b-d0c9945ba52e', 'They repel each other with a force of the same size', 'D', true, 3),
('836d39d8-18dc-5cc4-bf65-56292ffcf233', '7e913fa1-57ad-57be-8898-dbcea1cae1f6', 'Along wire 2', 'A', false, 0),
('67960bb9-487e-5272-9220-a9ee0d278947', '7e913fa1-57ad-57be-8898-dbcea1cae1f6', 'At right angles to the plane containing the two wires', 'B', true, 1),
('a0c39506-4d16-56a2-ba64-fc908097b95d', '7e913fa1-57ad-57be-8898-dbcea1cae1f6', 'Along the line joining the wires', 'C', false, 2),
('c60ef332-b410-538e-97b2-3cf89ad91977', '7e913fa1-57ad-57be-8898-dbcea1cae1f6', 'In the direction of the current in wire 1', 'D', false, 3),
('7d1dd1ac-ac06-5988-bcac-483e04b797d5', 'bcca6bf6-e146-51d2-ab7c-25512224d433', 'They are pushed apart', 'A', false, 0),
('6e0f1e96-b539-5b98-ada7-df1780cb6da5', 'bcca6bf6-e146-51d2-ab7c-25512224d433', 'Nothing happens', 'B', false, 1),
('748325c8-ed72-5d94-82df-f33f26a38d2d', 'bcca6bf6-e146-51d2-ab7c-25512224d433', 'They are pulled together', 'C', true, 2),
('f478782c-e8df-5073-be0e-416c77e4ef03', 'bcca6bf6-e146-51d2-ab7c-25512224d433', 'They twist apart', 'D', false, 3),
('4650b4f2-d43c-573b-bcd9-2b4c3755fe91', 'ad52d46f-bf63-5af5-b700-427c55cd02ff', 'Neither: the forces are equal in size', 'A', true, 0),
('87a80aab-6f3c-50eb-922d-fbac9cd628ab', 'ad52d46f-bf63-5af5-b700-427c55cd02ff', 'The one with the larger current', 'B', false, 1),
('d8526458-afa8-58c7-bc85-6529add4a3b0', 'ad52d46f-bf63-5af5-b700-427c55cd02ff', 'The one with the smaller current', 'C', false, 2),
('5cbdd81b-f2bf-5605-ba1a-de315c13667f', 'ad52d46f-bf63-5af5-b700-427c55cd02ff', 'The one that is longer', 'D', false, 3),
('4ddfba95-ce0a-5411-83fd-2de6e3a7a3c2', '05021df8-2911-58b3-90cc-e2d7b2550e8b', 'An attraction', 'A', false, 0),
('7876fd0b-3471-5ffb-829f-1d26aff0efc7', '05021df8-2911-58b3-90cc-e2d7b2550e8b', 'No force', 'B', false, 1),
